"""Render an honest summary of executed verification records."""
from pathlib import Path
import json,html
ROOT=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]
def read(name):return json.loads((ROOT/'validation'/name).read_text())
tokens=read('token-checks.json');browser=read('browser-checks.json');exports=read('export-checks.json')
text_pairs=[x['ratio'] for x in tokens['results'] if x['minimum']==4.5]
artifact=read('artifact-checks.json') if (ROOT/'validation/artifact-checks.json').exists() else None
artifact_html=f'<li>{artifact["htmlPages"]} HTML pages and {artifact["localLinksAndAssets"]} local links/assets checked; {len(artifact["errors"])} errors.</li>' if artifact else ''
artifact_link='<li><a href="artifact-checks.json">Static artifact checks</a></li>' if artifact else ''
motion=read('motion-runtime-checks.json') if (ROOT/'validation/motion-runtime-checks.json').exists() else None
motion_html=f'<li>Motion 13.4.0 and GSAP 3.15.0: {motion["passed"]} real-browser contracts passed, {motion["failed"]} failed, covering all {motion["recipes"]} recipes and the material signatures.</li>' if motion else ''
motion_link='<li><a href="motion-runtime-checks.json">Real-engine motion contracts</a> · <a href="motion-static-checks.json">Static motion contracts</a></li>' if motion else ''
rows=''.join('<li>'+html.escape(item['check'])+'</li>' for item in browser['checks'] if item['check']!='palette and material rendering')
page=f'''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><meta name="color-scheme" content="light dark"><title>Verification · Crystal</title><link rel="icon" href="../assets/icon.svg" type="image/svg+xml"><link rel="stylesheet" href="../assets/crystal-theme.css"><link rel="stylesheet" href="../assets/crystal.css"><link rel="stylesheet" href="../assets/site.css"><script src="../assets/tokens.js" defer></script><script src="../assets/crystal.js" defer></script><script src="../assets/docs.js" defer></script><link rel="stylesheet" href="../assets/controls.css?v=pill-focus-2"><script src="../assets/controls.js?v=pill-focus-2" defer></script></head><body><div class="shell"><header class="site-header"><a class="wordmark" href="../index.html" aria-label="Crystal design system"><span class="mark" aria-hidden="true"><svg aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><use href="../assets/icons.svg#crystal"/></svg></span>crystal <small>Design system</small></a><nav class="site-nav" aria-label="Main"><a href="../index.html#playground">Playground</a><a href="../index.html#foundations">Foundations</a><a href="../index.html#components">Components</a><a href="../motion.html">Motion</a><a href="../docs/principles.html">Specification</a><a href="../validation/report.html" aria-current="page">Verification</a></nav></header><main style="max-width:900px;margin:45px auto"><h1>Verification and limits</h1><p>Checks executed September 17, 2026. This is evidence about this reference package, not production application readiness or complete WCAG conformance.</p><h2>Executed checks</h2><ul><li>{tokens['checks']} solid-pair and bounded composite contrast cases; {len(tokens['failures'])} failures. Minimum normal-text result: {min(text_pairs):.2f}:1. Essential non-text cases use their separate 3:1 threshold.</li><li>All six palettes in both modes, scene navigation, appearance controls, preference restoration, reduced effects and keyboard dialog focus behavior exercised in the browser.</li><li>Responsive scenes at 320px and 390px, plus final material studies at 320px, checked for page overflow.</li><li>CSS and JSON files actually downloaded through the UI and inspected for the current configuration, both modes and updated material parameters.</li><li>Plastic opacity and inactive fallback, 40px Frost diffusion, and Resin appearance checked.</li><li>Five immutable Gather specification copies verified against their SHA-256 manifests and the original files.</li>{artifact_html}{motion_html}</ul><h2>Scope and limitations</h2><p>The contrast model checks Resin/Haze control labels with optical sheen beneath the protective fill, declared solid pairs, foundation combinations, 80%/79% content composites and RGB-corner backdrops with the fixed 20% Resin fill and mode-specific Stone fill and optical sheen. It is not a pixel-level audit of every possible image or layout. Native materials, screen readers, full zoom/assistive workflows, forced-colors rendering and cross-browser coverage remain adoption checks.</p><p>The HTTP preview was tested. The browser's URL policy blocked a direct file-URL test; no workaround was attempted. The files use relative local assets, but direct-file execution is not claimed as browser-tested.</p><p>The initial native dialog allowed Tab to leave the document for browser chrome. Explicit focus wrapping was added, then containment, Escape and focus return passed. The Harbor light contextual-text and Harbor dark glass extremes were corrected before the final contrast run.</p><h2>Evidence files</h2><ul><li><a href="token-checks.json">Token/composite results</a></li><li><a href="browser-checks.json">Observed browser checks and limitations</a></li><li><a href="export-checks.json">Downloaded export checks</a></li>{artifact_link}{motion_link}<li><a href="../reference/provenance.json">Preserved source manifest</a></li></ul><h2>Browser scenarios</h2><ul>{rows}</ul><h2>Historical captured previews</h2><p>These captures predate the latest Resin/Haze controls and material-driven component choreography. Use the live motion suite for the current rendering.</p><p><a href="../artifacts/crystal-motion.png">Interactive motion collection</a> · <a href="../artifacts/crystal-mirage-chromatic.png">Chromatic Mirage modal</a> · <a href="../artifacts/crystal-named-materials.png">Haze, Stone and Mirage</a> · <a href="../artifacts/crystal-content-blending.png">80% Haze over Resin</a> · <a href="../artifacts/crystal-desktop-dark.png">Desktop dark conversation</a> · <a href="../artifacts/crystal-mobile-light.png">Narrow light conversation</a> · <a href="../artifacts/crystal-material-hierarchy.png">Material studies</a></p></main><footer class="site-footer"><p>Crystal 1.0 · Reproducible evidence, bounded claims.</p><a href="../docs/adoption.html">Build and adoption guide</a></footer></div></body></html>'''
